{"type": "item", "run_id": "20260929T014630Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "09d1d26fa19dd694ec40f7bb", "title": "Holo4: powering generalist computer-use agents", "url": "https://huggingface.co/blog/Hcompany/holo4", "source": "Hugging Face - Blog", "published": "2026-09-28T09:44:05+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.7575, "worthiness_confidence": 0.97, "final_score": 0.7575, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 8278, "delivered": true, "summary": "H Company released Holo4, a series of agentic models (27B dense and 35B-A3B MoE) designed for generalist computer-use across GUIs, code, MCPs, and APIs without requiring separate models per interface. On OSWorld 2.0, Holo4-27B scores 61.7% versus Opus 5.5's 81.8%, achieving competitive performance at significantly lower cost through training on 10,000 tasks from their Agentic Task Factory. The key takeaway: unified multi-interface agents trained with supervised and reinforcement learning can match frontier closed models while reducing inference costs by orders of magnitude.", "jev_ms": 239.3, "jev_input_tokens": 2756, "jev_cost": 0.000115752, "llm_ms": 4191.6, "llm_cost": 0.003256, "errors": []}
